            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> I'm using this configuration to trigger the replace command. If I use piw the first replacement works well, but if I try to do (.) in the next word nothing happens.\n\nI can not reproduce. With `<Leader>p` prefix pressing `.` on some other word after `<Leader>piw` replaces the word as expected.\n\nI am pretty there is nothing wrong with 'mini.operators' here and this is a result of some config. Maybe there is a custom `.` override (see it with `:map .`)? Closing for now, but if you manage to reproduce with the minimal config (example is present in the issue), we can take a look at it.",
